Implementing Production-Grade RBAC in Argo CD
Objectives
Design and enforce a multi-tier RBAC policy in Argo CD that isolates permissions across developer, DevOps, and admin roles using the Casbin policy engine embedded in Argo CD
Validate access boundaries by testing each role's permitted and denied operations against scoped AppProjects and Applications
Diagnose and resolve RBAC misconfiguration using Argo CD's policy evaluation API and server-side audit logs
Prerequisites
Comfort with Linux command-line operations including file editing, process management, and reading structured log output
Conceptual understanding of Kubernetes RBAC (Roles, RoleBindings, ServiceAccounts) and how namespace isolation works
Familiarity with GitOps principles and the Argo CD application model (Applications, AppProjects, sync policies)
Lab Environment
You will work on a dedicated AWS EC2 Ubuntu instance provided by Al Nafi. The instance has a base Ubuntu installation; you will install all required tools in Task 1.

Task 1: Provision the Environment
Step 1.1: Install Container Runtime, Kubernetes Tooling, and Argo CD CLI
Your instance has no tooling pre-installed. You must bring up a single-node Kubernetes cluster using Minikube, then install the Argo CD CLI. The cluster must be reachable via kubectl before you proceed to Task 2.

Install Docker, kubectl, Minikube, and the Argo CD CLI. Verify each tool reports a valid version before continuing. The cluster must start with at least 4 GB of memory and 2 CPUs allocated to Minikube so that Argo CD's control-plane components have sufficient headroom.

