Task 3: Validate Access Boundaries and Audit Policy Decisions
Step 3.1: Execute Boundary Tests for Each Role
Your requirement is to programmatically verify that each user can perform exactly the operations the policy matrix in Step 2.1 permits, and is denied all others. Use argocd account can-i for pre-flight checks and direct CLI operations for live enforcement tests.

The interface contract below defines the shape of a validation harness you must implement as a shell script named rbac-validator.sh. You own the implementation; the contract defines what the script must accept and emit.

# Interface contract â implement this in rbac-validator.sh
#
# rbac_test_case()
#   Arguments:
#     $1  username        (string)  â local Argo CD account name
#     $2  password        (string)  â account password
#     $3  resource        (string)  â Argo CD resource type (e.g. "applications")
#     $4  action          (string)  â action verb (e.g. "sync", "create", "delete")
#     $5  object          (string)  â resource object path (e.g. "team-alpha/guestbook-alpha")
#     $6  expected_result (string)  â "allow" or "deny"
#   Returns:
#     Prints one line: "PASS" or "FAIL: <reason>"
#     Exit code 0 on PASS, 1 on FAIL
#
# rbac_run_suite()
#   Arguments: none
#   Behaviour: calls rbac_test_case for every row in the matrix below,
#              accumulates results, prints a summary table, exits non-zero
#              if any case fails
#
# Required test matrix (implement all rows):
#   alice  / AlicePass#2024  / applications / get    / team-alpha/guestbook-alpha  / allow
#   alice  / AlicePass#2024  / applications / sync   / team-alpha/guestbook-alpha  / allow
#   alice  / AlicePass#2024  / applications / sync   / team-beta/guestbook-beta    / deny
#   alice  / AlicePass#2024  / applications / create / team-alpha/*                / deny
#   alice  / AlicePass#2024  / applications / delete / team-alpha/*                / deny
#   bob    / BobPass#2024    / applications / create / team-alpha/*                / allow
#   bob    / BobPass#2024    / applications / delete / team-alpha/*                / allow
#   bob    / BobPass#2024    / repositories / create / *                           / allow
#   bob    / BobPass#2024    / projects     / create / *                           / deny
#   bob    / BobPass#2024    / clusters     / delete / *                           / deny
#   charlie/ CharliePass#2024/ projects     / create / *                           / allow
#   charlie/ CharliePass#2024/ clusters     / delete / *                           / allow
After implementing the script, run it and confirm all rows report PASS:

chmod +x rbac-validator.sh
./rbac-validator.sh
Confirmation: The summary table must show zero FAIL rows. Any FAIL indicates a policy rule gap that must be corrected in argocd-rbac-cm before proceeding.

Step 3.2: Audit Policy Decisions via Server Logs and the can-i API
Enable debug-level RBAC logging on the Argo CD server, trigger a denied action as alice, and capture the resulting log entry. Then use the argocd account can-i API to confirm the policy engine's decision matches the log evidence.

# 1. Enable RBAC enforcement logging
kubectl patch configmap argocd-cmd-params-cm -n argocd --type merge -p '{
  "data": {
    "server.log.level": "debug",
    "server.log.format": "json"
  }
}'

kubectl rollout restart deployment/argocd-server -n argocd
kubectl wait --for=condition=available --timeout=120s deployment/argocd-server -n argocd
# 2. Trigger a denied action as alice (attempt to sync team-beta app)
argocd login localhost:8080 \
  --username alice \
  --password "AlicePass#2024" \
  --insecure

argocd app sync guestbook-beta || true
# 3. Capture the RBAC enforcement log entry
# The log line will contain "enforcer" and the decision "false" for a deny.
kubectl logs -n argocd deployment/argocd-server --since=2m \
  | grep -i "enforc" \
  | tail -20
# 4. Confirm via the can-i API (re-authenticate as admin first)
ARGOCD_INITIAL_PASSWORD=$(kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret \
  -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 --decode)

argocd login localhost:8080 \
  --username admin \
  --password "${ARGOCD_INITIAL_PASSWORD}" \
  --insecure

# Each command prints "yes" (allow) or "no" (deny)
argocd account can-i sync   applications --as alice   "team-alpha/guestbook-alpha"
argocd account can-i sync   applications --as alice   "team-beta/guestbook-beta"
argocd account can-i create applications --as alice   "team-alpha/*"
argocd account can-i create applications --as bob     "team-alpha/*"
argocd account can-i delete projects     --as bob     "*"
argocd account can-i delete projects     --as charlie "*"
Confirmation: The can-i output must match the expected_result column in the test matrix exactly. Any mismatch means the policy in argocd-rbac-cm does not match your intent and must be corrected.

